# `fullouter` with rows missing on both sides: `c-999` has orders but no customer, `c-200` has a
# customer but no orders. The one `customerId` column is `coalesce(left, right)`, so it is never
# null (D-019).
mode: run
skip: `join` cannot run yet (M1-06, M1-09)
---- query
from '../../../data/orders.csv'
| where customerId in ('c-001', 'c-999')
| join kind = fullouter (from '../../../data/customers.csv' | where customerId in ('c-001', 'c-200')) on customerId
| project customerId, orderId, name
| sort by customerId asc, orderId asc
---- expected
customerId | orderId | name
string     | string  | string
-----------+---------+----------
c-001      | o-0015  | Ana Silva
c-001      | o-0024  | Ana Silva
c-001      | o-0030  | Ana Silva
c-001      | o-0031  | Ana Silva
c-200      | null    | Mo Haddad
c-999      | o-0007  | null
c-999      | o-0020  | null
